There is deliberately no Message-ID header on this mail. RFC 5322 only makes it a SHOULD,
and web forms that inject mail directly do sometimes omit it.

The plugin should fall back to the IMAP UID - qualified with the host, folder and
UIDVALIDITY - so the mail still gets a stable identity for duplicate detection. Look for a
`uid:` prefix instead of `msgid:` in the imap_mail_processed table.

Note also that the From header carries a bare address with no display name, so mailSenderName
should be absent from the process variables rather than empty.
